From 19e0af301fcf2f71c3da8ce4c415b6a83f906f5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cn <cn@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:16:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add China (CN) region support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the 国服 region to the launcher so it can install, update and sign
into World of Warcraft: Forever on NetEase's Chinese realms.

- GameRegion: add CN, and let the CN edition lock the region.
- WowClientDownloader: read the CN patch table from
  cn.version.battlenet.com.cn, which lists the same ARM64 build for every
  region and points the CN row at NetEase's CDN.
- .build.info: write the cn branch with CN/zhCN tags instead of enUS.
- Config.wtf: portal CN, agentUID wowf, zhCN text and audio.
- Login: the CN realms authenticate on cn.actual.battlenet.com.cn, so the
  browser-login host is mapped there; the sign-in domains (battlenet.com.cn,
  blizzard.cn and NetEase's SSO domains) are allowed, and third-party
  cookies are on. Password login stays available but CN drops it during
  credentials submission, so browser login is the default for CN.
- Chinese UI: the setup screen, dialogs, status and error text are in
  Simplified Chinese, and the app locale is pinned to zh-CN.
- Separate app: id app.wowforever.cn, its own game folder (WoW Forever CN)
  and hardcoded package paths replaced with BuildConfig.APPLICATION_ID, so
  it installs next to the international edition.
- App self-update is off, so the CN build is never replaced by an
  international APK.
